text	The README's install command reads `npm instal shop`, which npm doesn't recognize, so I'm correcting it to `npm install shop`.  
Bash	D=<craft>/skills/github; cat $D/tracker.md
Bash	D=<craft>/skills/github; gh label list; bash $D/scripts/collect.sh take-in 91 bug,debt README.md "npm instal" install
Bash	cat <tmp>/collect.UZl1MF
text	Issue #95 is a duplicate of #91, since both trace back to the same `npm instal shop` typo in README.md; I'm copying its stack trace to #91 before closing #95.  
Bash	gh repo view acme/shop --json visibility --jq .visibility; gh repo view --json nameWithOwner,visibility
Write	<tmp>/tmp.Kmi4A10CFV/run1/comment-91.md
Bash	D=<craft>/skills/github; bash $D/scripts/worktree.sh 91 docs/91-fix-npm-install-typo
Bash	gh issue comment 91 --body-file <tmp>/tmp.Kmi4A10CFV/run1/comment-91.md && gh issue close 95 --duplicate-of 91 --comment "Same report as #91; what it adds is copied there."
ToolSearch	
EnterWorktree	
Bash	cat -n README.md; ls -a
text	I closed duplicate #95 and I am in the worktree now. Next I fix the README line.
Bash	sed -i '' 's/npm instal shop/npm install shop/' README.md && cat README.md && git diff --stat
text	The repository has no check command: there is no `package.json`, no Makefile and no CI. The closest check is to read the diff, which I did. Next is the review step.
Skill	craft:review-loop
Bash	git add README.md && git commit -q -m "docs: fix the npm install command in the README" && git log --oneline -2 && git merge-base origin/main HEAD
Agent	Review README diff
subBash	git diff a163998..HEAD && echo ---FILES--- && git ls-files && echo ---README--- && cat -n README.md
text	Round 1 found nothing. Next I push the branch and open the pull request.
Bash	gh pr list --state merged --limit 5 --json title; git push -q origin HEAD 2>&1 | tail -3
Write	<tmp>/tmp.Kmi4A10CFV/run1/pr-91.md
Bash	gh issue view 91 --json assignees,labels --jq '{a:[.assignees[].login],l:[.labels[].name]}'
Bash	gh pr create --assignee @me --base main --title "docs: fix the npm install command in the README" --body-file <tmp>/tmp.Kmi4A10CFV/run1/pr-91.md
text	I fixed the README on a new branch and pushed it, but I could not open the pull request. `gh pr create` failed with this error:  ``` fake gh: no answer for: pr create --assignee @me --base main --title docs: fix the npm install command in the README --body-file …/pr-91.md ```  The `gh` in this environment is a stub, and it has no response for creating a pull request. So the pull request is not open, and there is no merge to ask about.  **#91 README: the install command says npm instal.** The README told readers to run `npm instal shop`, and that command fails.  - **The fix:** `README.md:3` now says `npm install shop`. It is committed as `e15ae73 docs: fix the npm install command in the README` on the branch `docs/91-fix-npm-install-typo`, in its own worktree. - **Issues:** #91 is assigned to `kim` and has the label `in progress`. I closed #95 Installing shop by the README leaves the app without the module as a duplicate of #91. It reported the same `npm instal shop` line, and I first copied its stack trace into a comment on #91. - **Review:** this is a change to documents only, so it got one review round. A review subagent read the diff and found nothing. The rules for a README change call for no Codex read and no security review. The repository has no architecture file, and `craft:architecture` can write the first one. - **Check:** the repository has no check command. There is no `package.json`, Makefile or CI, so I read the diff instead. - **Docs:** the README is the change.  The pull request description is ready in `…/run1/pr-91.md`, with `Closes #91` and the `## Review` section. When `gh` can reach GitHub, this command opens the pull request:  ```bash gh pr create --assignee @me --base main --title "docs: fix the npm install command in the README" --body-file <tmp>/tmp.Kmi4A10CFV/run1/pr-91.md ```
